From d467454e4b9008bb731058c22380eb6e25dd8a4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iam <iam@iashur.internal>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 08:37:36 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] compositor: real frame timing -- honest
 Compositor_FrameTiming from measured values

GetFrameTiming filled the struct with hardcoded constants (TotalRenderGpu=9.0
etc.) -- OpenVR Benchmark reported exactly 1000/9.0=111.11 'FPS' at any
resolution and load (T217/T218): fiction. Now: real WaitGetPoses interval,
real blocked-wait duration, real Submit copy time, real xrEndFrame time;
TotalRenderGpuMs = the real CPU frame interval (xrizer cannot fence the
app's own GPU work -- documented compromise: a load-tracking number beats a
constant); honest zeros for the unmeasurable; 128-entry ring buffer;
GetFrameTimings implemented (was todo!() -- panicked any caller) honoring
the header's per-entry-stride contract; frames_ago honored (was ignored);
m_nNumDroppedFrames now written (was NEVER set -- games read stack garbage).
87+1 tests including 3 new.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
